Date: Wed, 16 Sep 2026 15:41:18 -0500
Subject: [PATCH 2/3] A term is judged at the valuation its session RAN under

`recordedValue` means WHAT THIS MINT OBSERVED (RootMint:435-446,
ActiveRegion:517-546).  For a SEED that is the valuation the session ran
under; for a FOCUSED replay it is not, because the wave's assignment is
planted at the mint AFTER the observation is read -- deliberately, so the
recording's own value stays distinguishable off the heap.  So every rule
that reads `recordedValue` as "the values this session executed at" is
unsound on a focused session.  Invariant 6 was one, and invariant 9 judges
`phiTerm` the same way.

39bedd768's HDFS-17960 wave 0 is the whole class in one corpus.  The focused
session `cb67875d1d896d4d-73ab772f` ran under
`rootAssignments:{"HDFS.CONFIG.SNAPSHOT_DELETION_ORDERED":"false"}` (its
`obligation.jsonl`; `obligation_query.smt2:6` asserts it; the plant
succeeded -- no ASSIGNMENT_UNPLANTED row in the wave) and minted
`recordedValue="true"`.  Invariant 6 evaluated its terms at `true` and
refused decisions 79, 140 and 145 -- `deleteSnapshot#u7#1` twice and
`removeSnapshot#u10#1` -- for stating the arm they actually took.  All
three verify at `false`.  Pass #8's corresponding session states the same
three outcomes and escaped only because its mint stated `""`, which is
unjudgeable; `f8543b075` filling that field turned two silently-unjudged
rows into three BLOCKING ones.

`RowInvariants.executed` is now the ONE notion of what a session ran, read
once per session and handed to both rules that judge a term:

* SEED: the mint read the root, so `recordedValue` is what ran.
* FOCUSED, MARKER or INTEGRAL: the wave's `rootAssignments` for that root.
* FOCUSED, CLOCK: the wave states a SKEW, never an instant, so the value is
  the mint's own reading plus `clockDeltas`, exactly as
  `RootMint.focusedRootValue` computed it.
* FOCUSED, a root the wave assigned nothing: the mint read it.

The ask is the FOCUS ROW, because it is the one row that states both
halves; `ImportGateMain.asks` joins it to the session by the worker's own
result row, the same join invariant 10 uses, and walks the workers once for
both.  A FOCUSED session whose focus row this epoch does not state is a
NAMED REFUSAL (`epoch/valuation`, BLOCKING) and never a fall back to
`recordedValue`: judging a counterfactual at the recording's valuation is
the defect being removed.  A root the ask cannot be stated for spells `""`,
which is the spelling every leaf this class cannot reach already has, so
the term goes unjudged rather than guessed.

Offline, `ImportGateMain --iteration`, full session sets (seed + 2 focused):

* refused run `final-39bedd768-17960`: 19 violations / 3 blocking ->
  16 / 0.  Exactly the three `field=outcome` rows are gone; the 16
  DIAGNOSTIC LINEAGE_LOST rows are byte-identical.
* pass #8 `final-f651c4879`: 19 / 2 with either jar, byte-identical gap
  files.  Its two blocking rows are invariant 8, `roots.jsonl seq=121
  field=recordedValue HDFS.CONFIG.SNAPSHOT_DELETION_ORDERED=`, one per
  focused session -- pass #8's own historical fact and not this rule's.
  Its focused terms are now JUDGED (the ask states `false` where the mint
  states `""`) and they hold.
* a session set with no obligation workers: 2 BLOCKING `epoch/valuation`
  rows, one per focused session, and no term judged.

`epoch/sessions` does not appear over a full set with either jar: that row
was the wave gate's cut-down session set, fixed separately.

46 @Test and the shell test green.

